WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:04.110
BETH: Most people express their
emotions through verbal communication,

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:08.440
or nonverbally through body language
and facial expressions and extreme

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:12.459
emotions can also be shown by
physical actions such as throwing or

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:17.320
punching something to show anger or by
hugging for affection or reassurance.

00:00:17.609 --> 00:00:21.490
JOE: This is not as easy for individuals
with autism who often find behaviour

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:26.299
is their main form communication,
whether it's good or bad and it’s

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.210
an expression of feelings and needs.

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:32.419
Individuals with autism might
behave in challenging ways because

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:34.849
they have trouble understanding
what's happening around them.

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:38.900
BETH: They may not comprehend what
other people are saying or communicating

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.785
non-verbally and they may have difficulty
communicating their own wants and

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:45.090
needs, which can lead to frustration.

00:00:45.599 --> 00:00:49.779
A behaviour that may seem unnecessary or
challenging to others, for the individual

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:54.660
with autism is there to get attention,
escape from something, gain access to

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:57.460
something or is automatic or sensory.

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:01.600
JOE: In autism all behaviour has
a functional element and behaviour

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:05.800
that challenges are often described
as communicating unmet needs.

00:01:06.309 --> 00:01:09.770
However, there may be a range of
factors that may be associated

00:01:09.789 --> 00:01:11.470
with behaviour that challenges.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:15.270
Behaviour can be considered a
problem if it limits access to

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:19.590
things a person enjoys, interferes
with learning new things, affects

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:23.589
interactions with others or limits a
family from enjoying things together.

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:27.259
BETH: Behaviours that challenge,
often form in childhood due to their

00:01:27.299 --> 00:01:31.110
inability to use vocal language
to express their wants and needs.

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:35.500
Children with autism may often struggle
with the word ‘no’ and will wait

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:36.680
for things to be brought to them.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.320
Behaviours that challenge, are
a way of managing frustration

00:01:40.349 --> 00:01:41.729
or coping with feelings.

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:45.669
JOE: Behaviours will persist, if
the behaviour itself meets the needs

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:49.450
of the individual or there is some
reinforcement of those behaviours.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:53.059
It is important to be aware
that behaviours serve a

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:54.830
function for an individual.

